      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this is correct. For example, if the existing pref specifies slice 1 with UIDs 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and the new pref specifies slice 2 with UIDs 1, 2, 3, 4, then the satisfiedByUids call will fail and both prefs will be added.\n\nPer discussion, I think we might have to fallback on the docuemented contract of setProfileNetworkPreferences, which is:\n\n     * Calling this API with a user handle defines the entire policy for that user handle.\n     * It will overwrite any setting previously set for the same user profile,\n     * and not affect previously set settings for other handles.\n\nI think this means that when setProfileNetworkPreferences sends a EVENT_SET_PROFILE_NETWORK_PREFERENCE message, it must include in that message the userId that was passed in (or, handleSetProfileNetworkPreference could deduce the user by looking at an arbitrary element in the list such as the first one, and rely on the fact that getUidListToBeAppliedForNetworkPreference ensures that all the preferences in the list are for the same userId; but in this case please add a comment).\n\nThen handleSetProfileNetworkPreference should clear all the policies for that userId before applying the changes.",
